                <head>86. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On January 28, 1961, President Kennedy nominated Henry R. Labouisse to succeed
                    James W. Riddleberger as Director of the International Cooperation
                    Administration (ICA). Labouisse, a lawyer, held various appointments with the
                    U.S. Government from 1941 to 1951. He served with the Mutual Security Agency
                    1951-1954 and was Director of the U.N. Relief and Works Agency for Palestine
                    Refugees 1954-1958. Labouisse’s nomination as ICA Director was approved by the
                    Senate on <hi rendition="#italic">February 22, and he was sworn in on March
                        1</hi>.</p>
            </div>
